## QUESTION 32: How does the audit correlation ID enable request tracing across services?

The correlation ID system provides **end-to-end request tracing by maintaining a unique identifier throughout the entire request lifecycle using AsyncLocalStorage, allowing all operations triggered by a single request to be linked together in audit logs and across distributed services**.

### 1. **Context Initialization in Middleware** (context.middlware.ts:12-40)
The correlation ID is extracted or generated at the request boundary:

```
apps/whk-wms/src/context/context.middlware.ts:12-40
@Injectable()
export class ContextMiddleware implements NestMiddleware {
  use(
    req: RequestWithContext,
    res: Response,
    next: NextFunction,
  ) {
    const userId = req.user?.id || "system";

    const correlationId =
      req.get("x-correlation-id") ||
      req.get("x-request-id") ||
      randomUUID();

    const ipAddress =
      req.get("x-forwarded-for") ||
      req.get("x-real-ip") ||
      req.ip ||
      req.socket?.remoteAddress;

    const userAgent = req.get("user-agent") || undefined;

    // Keep a request-scoped metadata object
    const operationMetadata: Record<string, any> = {};
    req.whkCorrelationId = correlationId;
    req.whkOperationMetadata = operationMetadata;

    this.contextService.run(
      { userId, correlationId, ipAddress, userAgent, operationMetadata },
      () => {
        next();
      },
    );
  }
}
```

- **Header extraction priority**: `x-correlation-id` → `x-request-id` → generates new UUID
- **Context wrapping**: Uses `contextService.run()` to wrap the entire request in AsyncLocalStorage
- **Metadata enrichment**: Captures IP, user agent, and creates empty metadata object for downstream enrichment

### 2. **AsyncLocalStorage Context Management** (context.service.ts:1-70)
Core context isolation mechanism:

```
apps/whk-wms/src/context/context.service.ts:1-70
interface RequestContext {
  userId: string;
  sessionId?: string;
  correlationId?: string;
  ipAddress?: string;
  userAgent?: string;
  operationMetadata?: Record<string, any>;
}

@Injectable()
export class ContextService {
  private asyncLocalStorage: AsyncLocalStorage<RequestContext>;

  constructor() {
    this.asyncLocalStorage = new AsyncLocalStorage<RequestContext>();
  }

  run(context: RequestContext, callback: () => void) {
    this.asyncLocalStorage.run(context, callback);
  }

  getCorrelationId(): string | undefined {
    const store = this.asyncLocalStorage.getStore();
    return store?.correlationId;
  }

  setCorrelationId(correlationId: string): void {
    const store = this.asyncLocalStorage.getStore();
    if (store) {
      store.correlationId = correlationId;
    }
  }

  getFullContext(): RequestContext | undefined {
    return this.asyncLocalStorage.getStore();
  }
}
```

- **AsyncLocalStorage**: Node.js feature that maintains context across async boundaries
- **Per-request isolation**: Each request gets its own context instance
- **Getter/setter pattern**: Allows services to read and update correlation ID mid-request
