### **Correlation ID Journey Summary**

| Stage | Component | Line | Action |
|-------|-----------|------|--------|
| **Extraction** | ContextMiddleware | 23-24 | Get from header or generate |
| **Storage** | ContextService | 22 | Wrap in AsyncLocalStorage |
| **Retrieval** | AuditInterceptor | 73-75 | Extract when needed |
| **Propagation** | SessionAuditTracker | 86 | Update context mid-request |
| **Persistence** | Reconciliation | 202 | Store with business data |
| **Logging** | Audit Service | 135 | Include in audit records |
| **Isolation** | AsyncLocalStorage | tests 164-224 | Independent per request |

`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
The correlation ID system achieves distributed request tracing through **three layers**: (1) **middleware extraction** captures or generates an ID at request entry, (2) **AsyncLocalStorage isolation** maintains the ID without needing to pass parameters through every function call (solving the "context threading" problem), and (3) **database persistence** links all artifacts (audit logs, reconciliation records, business entities) to a single correlation ID. This enables powerful debugging queries like "show me all database changes caused by request `audit_1234_5678`" without modifying service signatures or adding hidden parameters.
