### PubSub Transport Layer

**apps/whk-wms/src/providers/pubsub/pubsub.provider.ts (lines 1-160)**

The `PubSubProvider` implements environment-aware pub/sub routing:

- **Production/Staging**: Uses `RedisPubSub` with separate publisher/subscriber connections for horizontal scaling
- **Development/Test**: Uses in-memory `PubSub` for simplified testing

```typescript
private initializePubSub(): void {
  const nodeEnv = String(
    this.configService.get<string>("NODE_ENV", "development") || "development",
  ).toLowerCase();

  // Use in-memory PubSub for local/dev/test environments
  if (nodeEnv === "development" || nodeEnv === "test" || nodeEnv === "e2e") {
    this.logger.log(`Using in-memory PubSub for ${nodeEnv} environment`);
    this.pubSub = new PubSub();
    this.isRedisBacked = false;
    return;
  }

  // Use distributed RedisPubSub for production/staging
  try {
    const redisUrl = this.configService.get("REDIS_URL");
    // Create separate Redis connections for publisher and subscriber
    this.publisher = new Redis(redisUrl, { ... });
    this.subscriber = new Redis(redisUrl, { ... });
    this.pubSub = new RedisPubSub({
      publisher: this.publisher as any,
      subscriber: this.subscriber as any,
    });
    this.isRedisBacked = true;
  } catch (error) {
    this.logger.warn("Falling back to in-memory PubSub");
    this.pubSub = new PubSub();
  }
}
```

The provider implements `OnModuleDestroy` (lines 143-160) to gracefully close Redis connections on shutdown, with fallback manual cleanup if `pubSub.close()` fails.

