## QUESTION 35: What is the data flow when a location is already occupied during entry event processing?

When a location is already occupied during entry event processing, the system implements a **trust-but-log pattern** with automatic conflict resolution. Here's the complete data flow:

### Entry Event Routing

**apps/whk-wms/src/barrelEvent/barrelEvent.service.ts (lines 452-519)**

Entry and TransferIn events are routed through a unified handler that determines whether the location is a holding location or storage location:

```typescript
private async handleEntryOrTransferInEvent(
  data: any,
  tx?: any,
): Promise<{
  barrelEvent: any;
  storageLocation: any;
  holdingLocation?: any;
  bruteForceWarningToLog?: any;
}> {
  const eventTypeName = "Entry";

  const isHoldingLoc = this.isHoldingLocationString(data.locationString);

  if (isHoldingLoc) {
    const result = await this.createHoldingLocationEntry(data, tx, eventTypeName);
    return {
      barrelEvent: result.barrelEvent,
      storageLocation: null,
      holdingLocation: result.holdingLocation,
      bruteForceWarningToLog: (result as any).bruteForceWarningToLog,
    };
  }

  // Storage location - proceeds to processStorageLocationEntry
  return this.processStorageLocationEntry(data, tx, eventTypeName);
}
```

### Location Availability Validation

**apps/whk-wms/src/barrelEvent/barrelEvent.service.ts (lines 1730-1903)**

The system validates location availability **before** finding or creating the barrel:

```typescript
private async validateStorageLocationAvailability(
  tx: any,
  storageLocation: any,
  barrelSN: string,
  locationString: string,
  deviceName?: string,
  data?: any,
): Promise<{
  isPermissiveReentry: boolean;
  locationConflict: {
    occupyingBarrelId: string;
    occupyingBarrelSN: string;
    errorToLog: { ... };
  } | null;
}> {
  const existingBarrel = await tx.barrel.findFirst({
    where: { locationId: storageLocation.id },
  });

  if (existingBarrel) {
    if (existingBarrel.serialNumber === barrelSN) {
      // SAME barrel - check reentry mode
      const reentryMode = await this.featureFlags.evaluate<BarrelReentryMode>({
        key: FEATURE_FLAG_KEYS.BARREL_REENTRY_MODE,
        defaultValue: "strict",
        context: {
          kind: "device",
          key: deviceName || "unknown",
          barrelSN,
          locationString,
        },
      });

      if (reentryMode === "permissive") {
        return { isPermissiveReentry: true, locationConflict: null };
      }

      // Strict mode: throw BarrelReentryError
      const errorToLog = {
        errorLevel: EnumDeviceSyncErrorLevel.WARN,
        errorType: "BarrelReentryError",
        errorMessage: `The same Barrel (${barrelSN}) is already stored at this location: ${locationString}`,
        context: { barrelSN, locationString, eventType: data?.eventType, ... },
      };
      throw new BadRequestException(...);
```

**Location Already Occupied by Different Barrel (lines 1830-1903)**

When a different barrel occupies the target location, the system returns conflict information instead of throwing:

