This allows **per-device trust mode configuration** - some devices can operate in permissive mode while others use strict mode.

`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
Trust mode operates as a **graduated validation system**: strict mode enforces consistency (throws errors), permissive mode enables operational flexibility (allows idempotent operations). The system separates three trust concerns: (1) barrel reentry at same location (controlled by feature flag), (2) location occupation by different barrels (auto-resolved with warning), and (3) barrel creation from missing data (always warned). This layered approach allows operators to adjust tolerance for reentry errors without affecting other safety mechanisms like duplicate barrel detection or location conflict resolution.
