## QUESTION 37: What database constraints ensure data integrity for barrel-location relationships, and how does BarrelLocationConflictException prevent conflicts?

The system implements a **multi-layer constraint approach** combining database-level unique constraints with application-level validation to prevent barrel-location conflicts.

### Database Constraints for Location Uniqueness

**apps/whk-wms/prisma/schema.prisma (lines 36-56)**

The StorageLocation model defines a one-to-one relationship with Barrel:

```prisma
model StorageLocation {
  id                     String                   @id @default(cuid())
  createdAt              DateTime                 @default(now())
  updatedAt              DateTime                 @updatedAt
  warehouse              Int?
  floor                  Int?
  rick                   EnumStorageLocationRick?
  position               Int?
  locationPath           String?
  tier                   Int?
  globalId               String?                  @unique @default(cuid())
  typeField              Int?                     @default(1)
  warehouseConfigId      String?
  barrels                Barrel?                  // One-to-one: Only one barrel per location
  barrelAudits           BarrelAudit[]
  holdingLocations       HoldingLocation[]

  @@unique([warehouse, floor, tier, rick, position])
  @@index([warehouse])
}
```

**apps/whk-wms/prisma/schema.prisma (lines 60-110)**

The Barrel model enforces location exclusivity via a unique constraint on `locationId`:

```prisma
model Barrel {
  id                     String                   @id @default(cuid())
  createdAt              DateTime                 @default(now())
  updatedAt              DateTime                 @updatedAt
  serialNumber           String                   @unique
  harvestTime            DateTime?
  harvestedBy            String?
  entryTime              DateTime?
  entryBy                String?
  lot                    Lot                      @relation(fields: [lotId], references: [id])
  lotId                  String
  harvestedDate          DateTime?
  char                   Float?
  fillDate               DateTime
  recipe                 String
  globalId               String?                  @unique @default(cuid())
  itemId                 String?
  seasoning              Float?
  locationId             String?                  @unique              // Ensures only 1 barrel per location
  barrelItemId           String?
  cooperageCode          String                   @default("UNK")
  barrelOemCodeId        String?
  systemStatus           EnumBarrelSystemStatus?  @default(Confirmed)
  holdingLocationId      String?
  disposition            EnumBarrelDisposition?   @default(PendingDisposition)

  location               StorageLocation?         @relation(fields: [locationId], references: [id])
  holdingLocation        HoldingLocation?         @relation(fields: [holdingLocationId], references: [id])

  @@index([holdingLocationId])
  @@index([disposition])
  @@index([systemStatus])
}
```

**Constraint 1: Location Uniqueness**
- `locationId` has `@unique` constraint (line 79)
- Only ONE barrel can reference a StorageLocation at any time
- Attempts to assign the same location to two barrels will fail at database level

**Constraint 2: Composite Location Uniqueness**
- `StorageLocation` has `@@unique([warehouse, floor, tier, rick, position])` (line 56)
- Ensures no duplicate physical locations in the warehouse
- Combined with Barrel's locationId uniqueness = guaranteed single-barrel occupancy

### BarrelLocationConflictException

**apps/whk-wms/src/errorExceptions/barrel.exceptions.ts (lines 89-104)**

The exception prevents invalid state where a barrel has both location types:

