## **Circuit Breaker State Machine**

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                  CIRCUIT BREAKER STATES               │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                      │
│  CLOSED (Normal Operation)                           │
│  ├─ Failure Count: 0                                │
│  ├─ All requests allowed                            │
│  └─ On consecutive failures → OPEN                  │
│         │                                            │
│         ↓                                            │
│  OPEN (Failure Detected)                            │
│  ├─ Failure Count > threshold                       │
│  ├─ All requests rejected                           │
│  ├─ Recovery window: circuitBreakerResetMinutes     │
│  └─ After timeout → HALF_OPEN                       │
│         │                                            │
│         ↓                                            │
│  HALF_OPEN (Recovery Test)                          │
│  ├─ Single request allowed                          │
│  ├─ If succeeds → CLOSED (reset failure count)      │
│  └─ If fails → OPEN (increment failure count)       │
│                                                      │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│          SAFETY LIMIT CHECKS (Sequential)            │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                      │
│  Batch Start                                        │
│       ↓                                             │
│  1. checkSafetyLimits()  ← SQL function             │
│     ├─ batchNumber < maxBatchesPerSession?          │
│     ├─ iterations < maxIterationsPerSession?        │
│     ├─ elapsed time < maxProcessingTimeMinutes?     │
│     ├─ consecutiveEmpty < maxConsecutiveEmpty?      │
│     ├─ consecutiveErrors < maxConsecutiveErrors?    │
│     └─ canContinue?                                 │
│       ↓ (if NO)                                    │
│  🛑 CIRCUIT BREAKER TRIPS                          │
│       ↓ (if YES)                                   │
│  2. checkResourceLimits()  ← Process metrics       │
│     ├─ memory < maxMemoryUsageMB?                   │
│     └─ shouldAbort?                                │
│       ↓ (if YES)                                   │
│  🚨 EMERGENCY STOP                                  │
│       ↓ (if NO)                                    │
│  3. Process Batch                                   │
│       ↓                                             │
│  4. Update Metrics                                  │
│     ├─ Track consecutiveEmptyBatches               │
│     ├─ Track consecutiveErrors                     │
│     └─ Reset circuit breaker on success            │
│                                                      │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

