`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
The separation into two modules enforces **schema and semantic separation**—StorageLocation is a constraint-rich coordinate system (warehouse/floor/tier/rick/position hierarchy) where exactly one barrel occupies each space, while HoldingLocation is a simple label-based staging system where multiple barrels coexist. Rather than forcing a single generic "Location" model to handle both cases (which would require nullable fields and expensive validation), the application splits them with distinct models, services, and routing logic. This allows each module to optimize for its use case: StorageLocation adds caching because position lookups are extremely frequent during barrel movements, while HoldingLocation remains simple because transfers to staging are less common. The mutual exclusion constraint on Barrel.locationId and Barrel.holdingLocationId prevents the schema from ever representing impossible states like "barrel in both a rack AND a holding area."
