### 5. **Post-Authentication Error Handling**

If authentication fails, the handleRequest method decides whether to return the user or throw:

**Pattern (apps/whk-wms/src/auth/multi-strategy-auth.guard.ts:86-106)**
```typescript
handleRequest(
  err: any,
  user: any,
  info: any,
  context: ExecutionContext,
  status?: any,
) {
  if (err || !user) {
    const errorMessage = err?.message || info?.message || "No user found";
    this.logger.debug(`Authentication error: ${errorMessage}`);

    // Throw error to trigger the catch block in canActivate
    // where we can apply development fallback
    throw err || new UnauthorizedException(errorMessage);
  }

  this.logger.log(
    `User authenticated: ${user.username || user.email || "Unknown user"}`,
  );
  return user;
}
```

