### **CACHING ARCHITECTURE** (Lines 1–51, `apps/whk-wms/src/eventType/cached-event-type.service.ts`)

**Three-Tier Caching Data Structure:**

```typescript
/**
 * Cached EventType Service - TEC-838
 * 
 * Provides in-memory caching for EventType lookups to reduce database contention
 * during high-concurrency Android sync processing.
 * 
 * EventType is reference data that rarely changes, making it ideal for caching.
 * This dramatically reduces SERIALIZABLE transaction conflicts on the EventType table.
 */
@Injectable()
export class CachedEventTypeService implements OnModuleInit {
  // Tier 1: Cache Storage
  // Map<eventTypeName, EventType | null>
  // Stores actual EventType records + null results to prevent repeated misses
  private eventTypeCache = new Map<string, EventType | null>();  // Line 25

  // Tier 2: Timestamp Metadata
  // Map<eventTypeName, cacheTimestamp>
  // Tracks when each entry was cached for TTL validation (lines 27–28)
  private cacheTimestamps = new Map<string, number>();

  // Tier 3: Reverse Index
  // Map<typeId, Set<eventTypeName>>
  // TEC-1196: Tracks ALL cache key variants (names) for each type ID for invalidation
  // Multiple name variants ("Entry", "ENTRY", "entry") map to the same EventType ID
  private idToNameMap = new Map<string, Set<string>>();  // Line 33

  // Cache TTL: 10 minutes (600,000 ms)
  private readonly CACHE_TTL_MS = 10 * 60 * 1000;  // Line 36
}
```

**Cache Metadata Tracking:**
- **Tier 1**: Stores actual data + null sentinels (prevents repeated DB queries for non-existent types)
- **Tier 2**: TTL timestamps for automatic expiration (auto-refresh on first miss after expiry)
- **Tier 3**: Reverse index for bulk invalidation of all name variants pointing to same EventType ID

