### **CACHE LOOKUP STRATEGY** (Lines 108–140, `cached-event-type.service.ts`)

**HIT/MISS/EXPIRED Pattern with TTL Validation:**

```typescript
async findEventTypeByName(name: string): Promise<EventType | null> {
  const now = Date.now();
  const cachedTimestamp = this.cacheTimestamps.get(name);

  // Check if cache entry exists and is still valid
  if (cachedTimestamp && now - cachedTimestamp < this.CACHE_TTL_MS) {
    const cached = this.eventTypeCache.get(name);
    this.logger.debug(`Cache HIT for EventType: ${name}`);
    return cached ?? null;  // Line 116: Return cached (or null if cached entry was null)
  }

  // Cache miss or expired - fetch from database
  this.logger.debug(
    `Cache MISS for EventType: ${name}, fetching from database`,
  );
  const eventType = await this.eventTypeService.findEventTypeByName(name);

  // Update cache (store null results too to avoid repeated lookups)
  this.eventTypeCache.set(name, eventType);    // Line 127: Store result
  this.cacheTimestamps.set(name, now);         // Line 128: Record timestamp

  // TEC-1196: Track ALL name variants for this event type ID for invalidation
  // Different case variations ("Entry", "ENTRY", "entry") all map to same EventType
  if (eventType) {
    if (!this.idToNameMap.has(eventType.id)) {
      this.idToNameMap.set(eventType.id, new Set());
    }
    this.idToNameMap.get(eventType.id)!.add(name);  // Line 136: Add to reverse index
  }

  return eventType;
}
```

**Key Optimizations:**

| Feature | Purpose | Benefit |
|---------|---------|---------|
| Null result caching (line 127) | Cache miss sentinels | Prevents repeated DB queries for non-existent types |
| TTL validation (line 113) | Auto-refresh after 10 minutes | Balances freshness with query reduction |
| Reverse index (lines 133–136) | Track all name variants | Enables bulk invalidation of case variants |
| Return cached ?? null (line 116) | Distinguish HIT from MISS | Proper handling of null cache entries |

