## Layer 4: Bulk Resolve

**apps/whk-wms/src/androidSyncInbox/device-sync-error-reprocessor.service.ts:591-605**

Uses **unconditioned update** with NO safeguards:

```typescript
async bulkResolve(errorIds: string[], reason: string): Promise<number> {
  const result = await this.prisma.deviceSyncError.updateMany({
    where: {
      id: { in: errorIds },
      // NO status condition - updates ANY error with these IDs
    },
    data: {
      status: EnumDeviceSyncErrorStatus.RESOLVED,
      resolutionReason: reason,
    },
  });

  this.logger.log(`Bulk resolved ${result.count} errors. Reason: ${reason}`);
  return result.count;
}
```

**Concurrency Vulnerability**:
- ❌ **No condition check**: Updates regardless of current status
- ❌ **Idempotent but risky**: Re-resolving already-RESOLVED error succeeds silently
- ⚠️ **Race Window**: Multiple concurrent bulkResolve() calls on overlapping error sets will all succeed
- **Example Race Scenario**:
  ```
  T0: Admin A calls bulkResolve([error-1, error-2]) with reason="Fixed in prod"
  T1: Admin B calls bulkResolve([error-1, error-3]) with reason="Outdated error"
  T2: Both complete successfully, error-1 gets resolutionReason overwritten
  T3: Audit trail unclear - last writer wins on error-1
  ```

